#: ../../TESTING.md:1 47aaee5369dd4d2687fc7b22a5bc932f
msgid "Smoke tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../TESTING.md:3 26ac537c916f4ee4889e12c84fe8d630
msgid ""
"`smoke_v2.py` drives `ql-backend` over a real WebSocket and is the only "
"proof the service works; there is no unit-test target yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../TESTING.md:6 272c6511bb3a43829b32678b76c7ae6b
msgid "It checks two different kinds of thing, and the distinction matters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../TESTING.md:8 adb3f45b105e4d2baa786e584655d395
msgid ""
"**Numbers.** 369 rows of QuantLib's own published reference values — "
"European and American vanillas, barriers and knock digitals, forward-"
"start, compound, chooser, cliquet and two-asset basket options and the "
"four quanto shapes — each priced through the wire and compared against "
"the value the C++ test suite records, at the tolerance that test uses. "
"Neither the values nor the tolerances are typed in: `reference_tables.py`"
" is generated from `test-suite/*.cpp` by `extract_tables.py`, and the "
"generator is checked in beside its output. Transcribing a benchmark by "
"hand is how it quietly stops being one — a digit changes and the test "
"still passes, against the wrong number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../TESTING.md:19 d68ef559e3ef4bafb63c30ca5a077d3b
msgid ""
"Three of those rows have no table behind them. `chooseroption.cpp` "
"publishes its two values, and `cliquetoption.cpp` its one, as local "
"variables in the bodies of their test cases, so `extract_tables.py` reads"
" them out variable by variable — naming the C++ variable each field comes"
" from — rather than letting three constants be typed here. A pattern that"
" stops matching is a hard failure, which is the point: the alternative is"
" a stale `6.1071` that outlives the number it was copied from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../TESTING.md:26 111b46f2efa24bd7bcfe40b0388f81ce
msgid "Re-run the generator when the QuantLib checkout moves:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../TESTING.md:32 d5047448bfab48f9b0872d4c2d4c96e1
msgid "The diff is then the library's change rather than ours."
msgstr ""

#: ../../TESTING.md:34 2ae428c2b12b498f88155780cdd737c7
msgid ""
"**Behaviour.** One session's life — open, bump a quote, reprice off the "
"live graph, sweep a quote, cancel a batched Monte Carlo, close — plus the"
" rejections that keep a forgotten field from pricing on a default nobody "
"chose, and two sessions disagreeing by one day of theta. That last one is"
" the check that catches the wrong QuantLib being linked: without "
"`QL_ENABLE_SESSIONS` the two share one `Settings::evaluationDate()` and "
"agree exactly (DESIGN §2)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../TESTING.md:41 2ea918d6562a4c70ae18200f3c5e90cf
msgid ""
"Two of the behaviour checks are replays in disguise. A sweep that keeps "
"its final value is followed by a finite-difference request, which moves "
"the session to a sacrificial worker and rebuilds it from the session log;"
" the kept spot has to survive that, which is only true if the supervisor "
"folded it into the log. And a swap section builds an index that forward-"
"references the curve bootstrapped off it, then bumps a swap pillar and "
"checks the trade moves — through the rebootstrapped curve *and* the "
"relinked index, which a copy would not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../TESTING.md:50 7c07b8e58e4e4621b4cf6e997a9c6321
msgid ""
"It also benchmarks, which is the part worth reading: it cross-checks the "
"analytic quanto barrier prices against a PDE, because `testBarrierValues`"
" in `quantooption.cpp` asks for exactly that benchmark and never got one."
" The numbers, and what they do and do not establish, are in [the quanto "
"barrier benchmark](BENCHMARK.md). One of the three recorded values does "
"not reproduce."
msgstr ""

#: ../../TESTING.md:56 ce2fc0e39bd249c9acc8394effed0c40
msgid ""
"The three earlier scripts — `smoke_pricing.py`, `smoke_sessions.py` and "
"`smoke_quanto.py` — were `v1` clients. The service speaks `v2` now "
"(DESIGN §6.3), so they could not be left in place; everything they "
"covered is here, and the quanto tables and the PDE benchmark came across "
"intact."
msgstr ""

#: ../../TESTING.md:61 932443b8659f48d5bf8d67afd3563f56
msgid ""
"It needs Python bindings for the schema and a client library, neither of "
"which the repository carries:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../TESTING.md:73 d0c9ffaea75743cc8dcb381d516578ce
msgid "It prints one line per check and exits non-zero if any failed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../TESTING.md:75 cac046d3b78c43e08620e12e3d8d472a
msgid ""
"Regenerate the bindings whenever the `proto` submodule moves. They are "
"written to a directory outside the repository and nothing rebuilds them "
"for you, so a suite run against a stale copy fails on a field the service"
" is sending and the bindings have never heard of."
msgstr ""

#: ../../TESTING.md:80 2127309a8e51449bbae7636f91b57962
msgid ""
"Against a daemon started with `--token-file`, put the secret in "
"`QL_TOKEN` and every connection the suite opens carries it as an "
"`Authorization` header:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../TESTING.md:88 63bfa821be294c638b5e883c15152d4c
msgid ""
"The whole suite passes either way. One check reads differently: "
"`/healthz` stops reporting its connection and session counts once a token"
" is required, and the check asserts whichever shape applies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../TESTING.md:92 22268ac2b5884f85a1e571f83d59f94e
msgid "One check only runs when the daemon is started with a short resume window:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../TESTING.md:98 c24cbbd9e138465a9626eecb260a3e21
msgid ""
"The resume section otherwise proves that a session, and the calculation "
"running in it, survive a dropped socket — but the window *expiring* is a "
"wall-clock wait, and sixty seconds of it does not belong in a test run. "
"With a two-second window it is one more check."
msgstr ""

